  "grid_title": "KINDS OF BACK PAIN",
  "why": "Muscle strain (a pulled muscle): a common cause of back pain; most back pain improves within a few weeks. Herniated disc: the soft, jelly-like center of a disc pushes through its tough outer ring and presses on a nerve; a slipped disc is the most common cause of sciatica (pain down the leg). Lumbar spinal stenosis: the space for the nerves in the lower spine narrows, most often in adults over 60; standing and walking make it worse, sitting or leaning forward helps. Spondylolysis: a stress fracture of the pars interarticularis (a thin bridge of bone at the back of a vertebra), in teens whose sports repeatedly arch the lower back (gymnastics, football, weightlifting). Spondylolisthesis: a vertebra slips forward on the one below. Red flag (cauda equina syndrome): back pain with numbness around the genitals or bottom, or changes in bladder or bowel control, is an emergency: go to the ER. Back pain that doesn't improve after a few weeks: see a doctor.",
